{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x / 7 for unsigned x: u32\n  m = ceil(2^35 / 7) = 4908534053 (0x124924925, 33 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^35)\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*7 = 2^35 + e with e = 3 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^35 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^35), and x*e/2^35 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer\n  m has 33 bits, one more than u32: the usual sequence uses m - 2^32 = 0x24924925 and an add that cannot overflow:\n    C:    t = mulhi(x, 0x24924925); q = (t + ((x - t) >> 1)) >> 2;\n    in ucas: (u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32) + ((x - u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32)) >> 1)) >> 2\n  check: the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 7 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "magic", "ucas": "magic 7 u32", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "magic", "m": "ceil(2^35 / 7) = 4908534053 (0x124924925, 33 bits), shift s = 3", "q": "floor(x * m / 2^35)", "proof_granlund_montgomery": "m*7 = 2^35 + e with e = 3 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^35 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^35), and x*e/2^35 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer", "m_has_33_bits_one_more_than_u32": "the usual sequence uses m - 2^32 = 0x24924925 and an add that cannot overflow:", "c": "   t = mulhi(x, 0x24924925); q = (t + ((x - t) >> 1)) >> 2;", "in_ucas": "(u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32) + ((x - u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32)) >> 1)) >> 2", "headline": "x / 7 for unsigned x: u32"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 7 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)"}], "files": [], "text": "x / 7 for unsigned x: u32\n  m = ceil(2^35 / 7) = 4908534053 (0x124924925, 33 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^35)\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*7 = 2^35 + e with e = 3 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^35 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^35), and x*e/2^35 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer\n  m has 33 bits, one more than u32: the usual sequence uses m - 2^32 = 0x24924925 and an add that cannot overflow:\n    C:    t = mulhi(x, 0x24924925); q = (t + ((x - t) >> 1)) >> 2;\n    in ucas: (u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32) + ((x - u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32)) >> 1)) >> 2\n  check: the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 7 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}, "isError": false}}
