{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x / 10 for unsigned x: u32\n  m = ceil(2^35 / 10) = 3435973837 (0xcccccccd, 32 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^35)\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*10 = 2^35 + e with e = 2 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*10 + r, 0 <= r < 10.  Then x*m/2^35 = x/10 + x*e/(10*2^35), and x*e/2^35 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/10: it cannot carry r/10 <= 9/10 past the next integer\n  m fits u32:\n    C:    q = (uint32_t)(((uint64_t)x * 0xcccccccd) >> 35);\n    in ucas: u32((u64(x) * 0xcccccccd) >> 35)\n  check: the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 10 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 10 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "magic", "ucas": "magic 10 u32", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "magic", "m": "ceil(2^35 / 10) = 3435973837 (0xcccccccd, 32 bits), shift s = 3", "q": "floor(x * m / 2^35)", "proof_granlund_montgomery": "m*10 = 2^35 + e with e = 2 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*10 + r, 0 <= r < 10.  Then x*m/2^35 = x/10 + x*e/(10*2^35), and x*e/2^35 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/10: it cannot carry r/10 <= 9/10 past the next integer", "c": "   q = (uint32_t)(((uint64_t)x * 0xcccccccd) >> 35);", "in_ucas": "u32((u64(x) * 0xcccccccd) >> 35)", "headline": "x / 10 for unsigned x: u32", "details": ["m fits u32:"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 10 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 10 (C's truncating division) for t