{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 27, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x / 27 for unsigned x: u32\n  m = ceil(2^37 / 27) = 5090331611 (0x12f684bdb, 33 bits), shift s = 5\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^37)\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*27 = 2^37 + e with e = 25 <= 2^5.  Write x = q*27 + r, 0 <= r < 27.  Then x*m/2^37 = x/27 + x*e/(27*2^37), and x*e/2^37 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/27: it cannot carry r/27 <= 26/27 past the next integer\n  m has 33 bits, one more than u32: the usual sequence uses m - 2^32 = 0x2f684bdb and an add that cannot overflow:\n    C:    t = mulhi(x, 0x2f684bdb); q = (t + ((x - t) >> 1)) >> 4;\n    in ucas: (u32((u64(x) * 0x2f684bdb) >> 32) + ((x - u32((u64(x) * 0x2f684bdb) >> 32)) >> 1)) >> 4\n  check: the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 27 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 27 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 27, "ok": true, "cmd": "magic", "ucas": "magic 27 u32", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "magic", "m": "ceil(2^37 / 27) = 5090331611 (0x12f684bdb, 33 bits), shift s = 5", "q": "floor(x * m / 2^37)", "proof_granlund_montgomery": "m*27 = 2^37 + e with e = 25 <= 2^5.  Write x = q*27 + r, 0 <= r < 27.  Then x*m/2^37 = x/27 + x*e/(27*2^37), and x*e/2^37 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/27: it cannot carry r/27 <= 26/27 past the next integer", "m_has_33_bits_one_more_than_u32": "the usual sequence uses m - 2^32 = 0x2f684bdb and an add that cannot overflow:", "c": "   t = mulhi(x, 0x2f684bdb); q = (t + ((x - t) >> 1)) >> 4;", "in_ucas": "(u32((u64(x) * 0x2f684bdb) >> 32) + ((x - u32((u64(x) * 0x2f684bdb) >> 32)) >> 1)) >> 4", "headline": "x / 27 for unsigned x: u32"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{