{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 54, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x / 1000 for unsigned x: u32\n  m = ceil(2^38 / 1000) = 274877907 (0x10624dd3, 29 bits), shift s = 6\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^38)\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*1000 = 2^38 + e with e = 56 <= 2^6.  Write x = q*1000 + r, 0 <= r < 1000.  Then x*m/2^38 = x/1000 + x*e/(1000*2^38), and x*e/2^38 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/1000: it cannot carry r/1000 <= 999/1000 past the next integer\n  m fits u32:\n    C:    q = (uint32_t)(((uint64_t)x * 0x10624dd3) >> 38);\n    in ucas: u32((u64(x) * 0x10624dd3) >> 38)\n  check: the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 1000 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 1000 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 54, "ok": true, "cmd": "magic", "ucas": "magic 1000 u32", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "magic", "m": "ceil(2^38 / 1000) = 274877907 (0x10624dd3, 29 bits), shift s = 6", "q": "floor(x * m / 2^38)", "proof_granlund_montgomery": "m*1000 = 2^38 + e with e = 56 <= 2^6.  Write x = q*1000 + r, 0 <= r < 1000.  Then x*m/2^38 = x/1000 + x*e/(1000*2^38), and x*e/2^38 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/1000: it cannot carry r/1000 <= 999/1000 past the next integer", "c": "   q = (uint32_t)(((uint64_t)x * 0x10624dd3) >> 38);", "in_ucas": "u32((u64(x) * 0x10624dd3) >> 38)", "headline": "x / 1000 for unsigned x: u32", "details": ["m fits u32:"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 1000 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arith