{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 56, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x / 7 for signed x: i32\n  m = ceil(2^34 / 7) = 2454267027 (0x92492493, 32 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^34) for x >= 0, plus 1 for x < 0\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*7 = 2^34 + e with e = 5 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^34 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^34), and x*e/2^34 <= 1 because |x| <= 2^31, so the extra term is at most 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer\n  (for x < 0 the floor lands one below the truncated quotient, since e > 0: hence the + 1)\n  as i32, m = -1840700269 (negative: the sequence adds x back):\n    C:    t = mulhs(x, -1840700269) + x; q = (t >> 2) + ((uint32_t)x >> 31);   (mulhs: the high 32 bits of the signed product, which already divides by 2^32)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 56, "ok": true, "cmd": "magic", "ucas": "magic 7 i32", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "magic", "m": "ceil(2^34 / 7) = 2454267027 (0x92492493, 32 bits), shift s = 3", "q": "floor(x * m / 2^34) for x >= 0, plus 1 for x < 0", "proof_granlund_montgomery": "m*7 = 2^34 + e with e = 5 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^34 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^34), and x*e/2^34 <= 1 because |x| <= 2^31, so the extra term is at most 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer", "c": "   t = mulhs(x, -1840700269) + x; q = (t >> 2) + ((uint32_t)x >> 31);   (mulhs: the high 32 bits of the signed product, which already divides by 2^32)", "headline": "x / 7 for signed x: i32", "details": ["(for x < 0 the floor lands one below the truncated quotient, since e > 0: hence the + 1)", "as i32, m = -1840700269 (negative: the sequence adds x back):"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text":